hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15535","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Abu al-Huwayrith Hafs, of the offspring of Uthman ibn Abi al-As, narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yala ibn Kab narrated to me, from Maymunah bint Kardam, from her father Kardam ibn Sufyan, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a vow vowed in Jahiliyyah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Is it for an idol or for a sacrificial stone? He said: No, but for Allah the Blessed and Exalted. He said: Then fulfill for Allah the Blessed and Exalted what you assigned for Him, slaughter at Buwanah and fulfill your vow."
